Package: whelk
Architecture: any
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
Description: Unix shell built from first principles
 whelk is a Unix shell whose purpose is to make the operating system's process
 model visible rather than hide it: processes, file descriptors, pipelines,
 signals, job control, terminals, and an event loop, each built on primitives
 that were understood first.
 .
 It runs real command lines -- pipelines, redirection, parameter expansion,
 quoting, job control with jobs, fg and bg, line editing with history and
 completion -- but it is not a drop-in replacement for an interactive shell.
 It has no &&, ||, or ;, no globbing, no command substitution, no
 here-documents, and no multi-line input. Those are parsed and refused by
 name rather than mistaken for arguments, and are listed in whelk --help.
